[{"id":444,"name":"AlphaRAR.aRTS_clt_joint","kind":"Theorem","keyword":"theorem","module":"AlphaRAR.YDK2026.ARTSNormality","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"ff15ee544827099a","local":"d70d91ce6d91a5b0","content":"0526b862da729487"},"doc":"**Joint central limit theorem for the aRTS design**, equation (9) of Theorem 4.2 (ii) of the\npaper, fully self-contained. From the `aRTS` design bundle — an `IsAlgEnvSeq` sequence, Condition\n**A** (the kernel `L²` bound `hνk`), a simplex-valued target `T` that is `LipschitzWith K`\n(Condition **B**), the algorithm-level predicate `IsARTS`, `α ∈ [0,1)`, the non-sparsity `hTpos`,\nand the first-order differentiability of `T` at `θ` with Jacobian `G` (`hTderiv`) — the `√n`-scaled\njoint vector `(√n(N_n/n - v), √n(ρ̂_n - v))` converges weakly to the block-Gaussian `𝒩(0, Ω)`, with\nevery block equal to `G · diag(V_k / v_k) · Gᵀ` with `V_k = Var[id; ν k]`, and\n`v_k = T ν.means k`.\n\nThe `aRTS` instantiation of `clt_joint_of_hitting` at the last under-sampling time: the throttle is\n`throttle_of_isARTS` (from `IsARTS`), the consistency smallness is `aRTS_smallness_all`, and the\n`o_p`-smallness is `aRTS_smallness_op`, both automatic because `N_ℓ - ℓ ρ̂_ℓ ≤ 0` at that time\n(`preliminary_small`). ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSingletonClass","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSingletonClass 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,24,"MeasurableSingletonClass"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Prob